  "_purpose": "Registry of load-bearing numbers cited in docs. tools/count_truth.py recomputes each value from its authoritative source and fails when a cited file no longer states the current value. The checker NEVER edits docs - drift is fixed by a human doc edit. STATED LIMIT (measured phase 43): a claim asserts that a cited file states the current value SOMEWHERE, not that every restatement in that file agrees. A doc carrying the same number twice stays green if one copy drifts. That is deliberate — several docs restate a historical figure beside the current one on purpose (e.g. the phase-38 correction narrative) — but it means count_truth is a floor, not a proof of internal consistency.",
